Grove PATCH-35: confirm ZANO's host-wallet identity on every node start

PATCH-17 gave ZanoInterface a wrong-wallet guard: before every spend on the
main (host) wallet-rpc connection, _confirmMainWalletIdentity re-reads the live
address and refuses unless it equals _cached_main_wallet_address -- including
when that is None, so "never confirmed" fails closed. The only assignment of the
cache was in initialiseWallet's _external_main_wallet branch.

A running node never calls initialiseWallet for ZANO. Its callers are
bin/prepare.py (a separate, first-time process), reseedWallet (a manual UI
action) and XMR-only debug code. So on every real Grove node the cache stayed
None for the node's whole life, and EVERY spend from the shared ZANO wallet was
refused: publishBLockTx and both withdrawCoin branches.

WHAT IT COST (2026-09-13, mainnet)

The first funded ZANO<>LTC swap. This node bid (sends ZANO). The offerer's LTC
lock confirmed; every attempt to publish the ZANO lock logged

    main wallet-rpc connection reports Zx..., expected confirmed identity None;
    refusing to send

100 times over 18 hours, across 13 engine restarts, none of which logged
initialiseWallet's own "ZANO main wallet is host-managed" line. The offerer
refunded through the lock-refund path. Nothing was lost -- the ZANO was never
sent -- but no ZANO-sending swap could ever have succeeded on this engine.

WHY XMR NEVER HAD IT, AND WHY THE SUITE STAYED GREEN

XMRInterface caches in openWallet (PATCH-8), and every main-wallet path opens the
default wallet first, so the node confirms at its first balance read or send.
ZanoInterface.openWallet is a no-op -- Zano has no open_wallet RPC -- so the
equivalent moment never came.

verify-zano-interface.py section 3 called initialiseWallet directly on a stub
and checked the cache: it proved the method caches, not that the node ever calls
it. The regtest matrix does not set external_main_wallet, which makes the guard a
no-op, so "ZANO 8/8" ran with the guard off.

THE FIX

_cacheMainWalletIdentityIfUnset: confirm once, while still None, from a
non-spend path, under the same rule as XMRInterface.openWallet. Called from
unlockWallet, which the node runs at every start, and from getWalletInfo, the
periodic read, so a host wallet that was briefly unreachable at unlock is still
confirmed before any spend. It is never called from inside the guard: a guard
that fills its own reference from the live read it is about to compare against
would pass for any wallet.

Unchanged: a wallet swapped AFTER confirmation is still refused, a second unlock
does not re-pin a different wallet, and a non-Grove deployment
(external_main_wallet False) makes no extra RPC call.

Verified by verify-zano-interface.py section 10, which starts from a fresh
interface that never ran initialiseWallet. Its negative control reproduces the
2026-09-13 refusal on an engine without this patch.

Scope: ZANO only. ZEPH inherits XMRInterface.openWallet's confirmation;
verify-zeph-host-wallet.py section 13 proves it on a restarted node.

Upstream candidate: no. ZanoInterface is Grove's own module (PATCH-15).

Regenerated 2026-09-17 on basicswap v0.18.9 (5471e609): the hand-edited body had hunk line counts that `git apply` rejects ("corrupt patch at line 113"), so check-basicswap-upstream.mjs reported this patch, and 0037 after it, as BREAK on every tag, while apply-engine-patches.mjs (which ignores hunk counts) applied it. The change is the same.

